invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_field.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: inverting the mask inverts the conditional subtraction of the
  wide field: a value is reduced exactly when it is already below p and
  left alone when it is not, so every sum and every Montgomery product
  leaves the field. bin/p256_equiv_test compares every wide field routine
  with p256_field.c's on the same limbs, and
  proof/p256_wide_field_harness.c fails on it for any limbs at all.

--- old
    uint64_t keep = p256_wide_mask(borrow & (high ^ 1U));
--- new
    uint64_t keep = p256_wide_mask((borrow & (high ^ 1U)) ^ 1U);
